.policy "python-practice-contextmanager-cleanup-skipped" revision 1
.description "Release what a @contextmanager generator acquired in a try/finally around its yield; an exception in the with-block skips code after the yield."
.language python
.mode log
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. contextlib runs a generator context manager up to its `yield`, runs the with-block,
// and, when the block raises, throws the exception in at the `yield`. Code after the yield then runs only if a
// handler around the yield catches the exception and goes on: the lock stays held, the file, cursor or connection
// leaks, the temp dir stays, the patched attribute, thread-local, environment variable, signal handler, alarm,
// sys.path entry or working directory stays changed for every later caller.
// It reports, outside test code, a `yield` in the own frame of a def decorated with contextlib.contextmanager or
// asynccontextmanager (resolved through imports, aliases included) when a release follows it on the normal path: in
// a later statement of a block that holds the yield, with no `return` or `raise` between them, and no handler
// between them that swallows the exception. Only two things swallow it: an `except` that catches everything
// (bare, Exception, BaseException) and neither re-raises nor returns, and `with contextlib.suppress(Exception)`. A
// `finally` runs its own body and re-raises, a narrow or re-raising `except` and any other `with` let the exception
// through: code after them is skipped. A release is:
//   - a call `X.m(...)` with m one of close, aclose, release, unlock, shutdown, stop, terminate, kill, disconnect,
//     dispose, rollback, cleanup, unlink; not `X.cleanup()` of a tempfile.TemporaryDirectory, whose finalizer
//     removes the directory as soon as the generator's frame is dropped;
//   - os.remove(), os.unlink(), os.rmdir(), shutil.rmtree();
//   - `X.reset(...)` or `X.restore(...)` when, before the yield, the def called a method of X or bound the
//     argument it passes (`token = var.set(v); yield; var.reset(token)`);
//   - `T = old` (T an attribute or subscript) when, before the yield, the def saved `old = T`, by T's text:
//     `orig = engines["jinja2"].env.autoescape; ...; yield; engines["jinja2"].env.autoescape = orig`;
//   - `T = False` when, before the yield, the def set `T = True` (True, False, None either way round);
//   - `del T` or `delattr(o, "a")` of an attribute or subscript the def set before the yield:
//     `_context.call = Call(); yield; del _context.call`, `sys.modules[n] = m; yield; del sys.modules[n]`;
//   - a write to os.environ: `os.environ[k] = old`, `del os.environ[k]`, os.environ.pop(), os.environ.update();
//   - a removal from a container the def added to before the yield, on the same receiver by its text: an add verb
//     (append, appendleft, insert, add, extend, push, register, subscribe, attach, install, or a name starting
//     with one: addHandler, add_listener) before, a remove verb (remove, pop, popleft, discard, clear, unregister,
//     unsubscribe, detach, uninstall, or a name starting with one: removeHandler) after:
//     `sys.path.insert(0, p); yield; sys.path.remove(p)`; and `X.pop(k)` after `X[k] = v`;
//   - a paired call: a call statement after the yield to the same function as a call before it (by sym_of, else
//     by its dotted text) with as many positional arguments, where the call before is a statement of its own or
//     the whole value of an assignment, and the function is neither a builtin nor a class of the run (a builtin
//     or a constructor computes a value, it does not set state). Either
//       restore: the call after passes, at one position, a name that holds the state read before the set (bound,
//       before the call before, to a call that is not a builtin or a class, an attribute or a subscript), where
//       the call before passed something else, and the other positions are the same text:
//       `old = get_user(); set_user(u); yield; set_user(old)`, `old = signal.signal(s, h); ...; signal.signal(s,
//       old)`, `old = os.getcwd(); os.chdir(p); yield; os.chdir(old)`;
//       reset: every argument of the call after is a neutral constant (0, None, False, or a named constant such
//       as logging.NOTSET or signal.SIG_DFL) and the arguments differ from the call before:
//       `signal.alarm(n); yield; signal.alarm(0)`, `logging.disable(CRITICAL); yield; logging.disable(NOTSET)`.
//   @contextmanager
//   def held(lock):
//       lock.acquire(); yield lock; lock.release()               reported at the yield
//       lock.acquire(); try: yield lock finally: lock.release()  not reported
//       try: yield c except Exception: c.rollback(); raise       not reported: commit is not a release, it is
//       c.commit()                                                 meant to run only on success
//       try: yield except ValueError: raise                      reported: a narrow except lets the error through
//       lock.release()
//       if lock is None: yield; return                           not reported: the release is unreachable from it
// Left alone: code after the yield that commits, flushes, enqueues, logs or records success (not a release);
// `X.reset()` or `del T` of something the def did not touch before the yield; a call computed before and after the
// yield (`label = str(key); yield label; log.info("%s", str(key))`: a builtin, and its value is used); a paired call
// whose arguments are the same, or whose later argument is no saved state (`notify("start"); yield;
// notify("end")`, `bar.update(0); yield; bar.update(100)`); lifespan functions (named `*lifespan*`, or passed as
// `lifespan=` anywhere in the run), whose shutdown is the server's; pytest fixtures (pytest runs the code after a
// fixture's yield also when the test fails); a yield in a nested def or lambda; a `contextmanager` decorator that is
// not contextlib's; test files.
// Name lists: the release methods and the add/remove verbs are names because a library container or resource
// type is not decidable from the call; everything else is by resolution or by the def's own writes.
// Gaps: a release in a helper the def calls after the yield (`self._teardown()`) is not followed; a release that
// is meant to be skipped on error (a marker file left behind on purpose so the next run retries) is reported, and
// the message says to leave it; a paired call whose later argument is a named constant used as an event, not a
// state (`emit(EVENT_START); yield; emit(EVENT_END)`), reads as a reset; a logging call that logs a saved value at
// the position where the call before logged another (`log.info(new); yield; log.info(old)`) reads as a restore;
// a with-statement whose own exit swallows exceptions (other than contextlib.suppress) is not known to.

#include "lib/python_practice.rerail"

.violation CleanupSkipped(at: node, fx: symbol, what: symbol, r: node)
    "`{what}` (line {r.line}) is skipped when the with-block of `{fx}` raises, so what it releases stays held or changed. Move it into a finally around the yield, unless it must run only on success."
CleanupSkipped(y, fx, what, r) :- ccs_yield(y, f), r = min o : { ccs_after(y, f, o) }, ccs_release(r, f, what),
    def_name(f, fx).

// ccs_yield(y, f): y is a yield of contextmanager f, outside test code, and f is not a lifespan.
.decl ccs_yield(y: node, f: node)
ccs_yield(y, f) :- pp_cm_yield(y, f), pp_live(y), !ccs_lifespan(f).
// ccs_lifespan(f): an ASGI lifespan: its shutdown is the server's, judged elsewhere.
.decl ccs_lifespan(f: node)
ccs_lifespan(f) :- pp_cm_def(f), def_name(f, x), contains("lifespan", x).
ccs_lifespan(f) :- kind(ka, "keyword_argument"), field(ka, "name", n), text(n, "lifespan"), field(ka, "value", v0),
    unparen(v0, v), sym_of(v, q), qualname(f, q), pp_cm_def(f).

// ccs_after(y, f, r): release r, in f's own frame, runs after the yield y on the normal path only: a later
// statement of a block that holds y, with no return or raise between them and no handler between them that
// swallows the exception thrown in at y.
.decl ccs_after(y: node, f: node, r: node)
ccs_after(y, f, r) :- ccs_yield(y, f), ccs_release(r, f, _), ccs_stmt(y, sy, b), ccs_stmt(r, sr, b), child(b, sy, i),
    child(b, sr, j), i < j, !ccs_exit_between(y, b, j), !ccs_swallowed_in(y, sy).
// ccs_stmt(n, st, b): python/flow's stmt_of, for yields and releases only: st is the statement of block b that
// holds n (or is n).
.decl ccs_point(n: node)
ccs_point(y) :- ccs_yield(y, _).
ccs_point(r) :- ccs_release(r, _, _).
.decl ccs_stmt(n: node, st: node, b: node)
ccs_stmt(n, st, b) :- ccs_point(n), within(n, st), child(b, st, _), kind(b, "block").
ccs_stmt(n, n, b) :- ccs_point(n), child(b, n, _), kind(b, "block").
// ccs_exit_between(y, b, j): from y, a return or raise leaves before statement j of block b: one later than y's own
// statement in a block inside b that holds y, or before j in b itself.
.decl ccs_exit_between(y: node, b: node, j: number)
ccs_exit_between(y, b, j) :- ccs_yield(y, _), ccs_stmt(y, sy, b), child(b, sy, i), child(b, s, k), i < k,
    ccs_exit(s), child(b, _, j), k < j.
ccs_exit_between(y, b, j) :- ccs_yield(y, _), ccs_stmt(y, _, b), ccs_stmt(y, sy2, b2), within(b2, b),
    child(b2, sy2, i2), child(b2, s, k), i2 < k, ccs_exit(s), child(b, _, j).
.decl ccs_exit(s: node)
ccs_exit(s) :- kind(s, "return_statement").
ccs_exit(s) :- kind(s, "raise_statement").

// ---- handlers that swallow ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ccs_swallowed_in(y, sy): inside statement sy (or at it), a handler around y swallows the exception thrown in at
// y, so code after sy runs on error too.
.decl ccs_swallowed_in(y: node, sy: node)
ccs_swallowed_in(y, sy) :- ccs_stmt(y, sy, _), ccs_swallow(y, t), (t = sy ; within(t, sy)).
// ccs_swallow(y, t): t, in y's frame, holds y in its body and swallows what y raises: a try with an except that
// catches everything and neither re-raises nor returns, or `with contextlib.suppress(Exception)`.
.decl ccs_swallow(y: node, t: node)
ccs_swallow(y, t) :- ccs_yield(y, f), kind(t, "try_statement"), field(t, "body", tb), within(y, tb), pp_frame(t, f),
    child(t, x, _), ccs_catches_all(x), !ccs_handler_exits(x).
ccs_swallow(y, w) :- ccs_yield(y, f), kind(w, "with_statement"), field(w, "body", wb), within(y, wb), pp_frame(w, f),
    within(c, w), !within(c, wb), kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", fn), sym_of(fn, "contextlib.suppress"),
    posarg(c, _, e), caught(e, q), ccs_catch_all(q).
.decl ccs_catch_all(q: symbol)
ccs_catch_all("builtins.BaseException"). ccs_catch_all("builtins.Exception").
// ccs_catches_all(x): except clause x catches everything: bare (a comment beside it, `except:  # noqa`, still
// bare), or naming Exception or BaseException.
.decl ccs_catches_all(x: node)
ccs_catches_all(x) :- kind(x, "except_clause"), count : { child(x, e, _), !kind(e, "block"), !kind(e, "comment") } = 0.
ccs_catches_all(x) :- catches(x, q), ccs_catch_all(q).
// ccs_handler_exits(x): except clause x re-raises or returns somewhere in it, so the code after its try is skipped
// on that path.
.decl ccs_handler_exits(x: node)
ccs_handler_exits(x) :- kind(x, "except_clause"), within(s, x), ccs_exit(s).

// ---- releases ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ccs_release(r, f, what): r, in contextmanager f's own frame, undoes something; what names it for the message.
.decl ccs_release(r: node, f: node, what: symbol)
ccs_release(c, f, x) :- ccs_call_in(c, f), field(c, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, o, m), ccs_release_method(m),
    !ccs_tempdir(o, f, m), text(c, x).
ccs_release(c, f, x) :- ccs_call_in(c, f), field(c, "function", fn), sym_of(fn, q), ccs_release_q(q), text(c, x).
ccs_release(c, f, x) :- ccs_call_in(c, f), field(c, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, o, m), (m = "reset" ; m = "restore"),
    ccs_touched_before(c, f, o), text(c, x).
ccs_release(a, f, s) :- ccs_attr_restore(a, f), text(a, s).
ccs_release(s, f, t) :- ccs_environ_write(s, f), text(s, t).
ccs_release(a, f, s) :- ccs_flag_reset(a, f), text(a, s).
ccs_release(d, f, t) :- ccs_unset(d, f), text(d, t).
ccs_release(c, f, t) :- ccs_unregister(c, f), text(c, t).
ccs_release(c, f, t) :- ccs_restore_call(c, f), text(c, t).
ccs_release(c, f, t) :- ccs_reset_call(c, f), text(c, t).
.decl ccs_call_in(c: node, f: node)
ccs_call_in(c, f) :- kind(c, "call"), pp_frame(c, f), pp_cm_def(f).
.decl ccs_release_method(m: symbol)
ccs_release_method("close"). ccs_release_method("aclose"). ccs_release_method("release").
ccs_release_method("unlock"). ccs_release_method("shutdown"). ccs_release_method("stop").
ccs_release_method("terminate"). ccs_release_method("kill"). ccs_release_method("disconnect").
ccs_release_method("dispose"). ccs_release_method("rollback"). ccs_release_method("cleanup").
ccs_release_method("unlink").
.decl ccs_release_q(q: symbol)
ccs_release_q("os.remove"). ccs_release_q("os.unlink"). ccs_release_q("os.rmdir"). ccs_release_q("shutil.rmtree").

// ---- what the def did before its yield ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ccs_assign(f, a, l, r): assignment `l = r` in contextmanager f's own frame. ccs_pre_assign / ccs_post_assign: one
// that comes before / after a yield of f.
.decl ccs_assign(f: node, a: node, l: node, r: node)
ccs_assign(f, a, l, r) :- kind(a, "assignment"), pp_frame(a, f), pp_cm_def(f), field(a, "left", l), field(a, "right", r).
.decl ccs_pre_assign(f: node, a: node, l: node, r: node)
ccs_pre_assign(f, a, l, r) :- ccs_assign(f, a, l, r), pp_cm_yield(y, f), earlier(a, y).
.decl ccs_post_assign(f: node, a: node, l: node, r: node)
ccs_post_assign(f, a, l, r) :- ccs_assign(f, a, l, r), pp_cm_yield(y, f), earlier(y, a).
// ccs_pre_name(f, v, y): name v is bound in f before yield y.
.decl ccs_pre_name(f: node, v: symbol, y: node)
ccs_pre_name(f, v, y) :- ccs_assign(f, a, l, _), kind(l, "identifier"), text(l, v), pp_cm_yield(y, f), earlier(a, y).
// ccs_arg_name(c, v): call c passes the name v.
.decl ccs_arg_name(c: node, v: symbol)
ccs_arg_name(c, v) :- ccs_call_in(c, _), field(c, "arguments", l), child(l, a, _), kind(a, "identifier"), text(a, v).

// ccs_tempdir(o, f, m): `o.cleanup()` with o a name f bound to tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(...): its finalizer
// removes the directory when the generator's frame drops it, so a skipped cleanup() leaves nothing behind.
.decl ccs_tempdir(o: node, f: node, m: symbol)
ccs_tempdir(o, f, "cleanup") :- ccs_call_in(c, f), field(c, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, o, "cleanup"),
    kind(o, "identifier"), text(o, v), ccs_tempdir_name(f, v).
.decl ccs_tempdir_name(f: node, v: symbol)
ccs_tempdir_name(f, v) :- ccs_assign(f, _, l, r), kind(l, "identifier"), text(l, v), kind(r, "call"),
    field(r, "function", rf), sym_of(rf, "tempfile.TemporaryDirectory").
// ccs_touched_before(c, f, o): `o.reset(...)`/`o.restore(...)` call c undoes a change made before a yield of f: f
// called a method of o there (by o's dotted text), or bound the name c passes (`token = var.set(v)`).
.decl ccs_touched_before(c: node, f: node, o: node)
ccs_touched_before(c, f, o) :- ccs_call_in(c, f), field(c, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, o, m),
    (m = "reset" ; m = "restore"), dotted_expr(o, d), ccs_pre_recv(f, d, y), earlier(y, c).
ccs_touched_before(c, f, o) :- ccs_call_in(c, f), field(c, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, o, m),
    (m = "reset" ; m = "restore"), ccs_arg_name(c, v), ccs_pre_name(f, v, y), earlier(y, c).
.decl ccs_pre_recv(f: node, d: symbol, y: node)
ccs_pre_recv(f, d, y) :- ccs_call_in(c, f), field(c, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, o, _), dotted_expr(o, d),
    pp_cm_yield(y, f), earlier(c, y).
// ccs_attr_restore(a, f): `T = old` after a yield of f, with T an attribute or a subscript, where `old = T` came
// before it (compared by T's text).
.decl ccs_attr_restore(a: node, f: node)
ccs_attr_restore(a, f) :- ccs_post_assign(f, a, l, r), (kind(l, "attribute") ; kind(l, "subscript")), text(l, d),
    kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, v), ccs_saved(f, v, d).
.decl ccs_saved(f: node, v: symbol, d: symbol)
ccs_saved(f, v, d) :- ccs_pre_assign(f, _, l, r), kind(l, "identifier"), text(l, v), text(r, d).
// ccs_flag_reset(a, f): `T = False` after a yield of f, where `T = True` came before it (T an attribute or a
// subscript, compared by its text; True, False and None, either way round): a flag the def raised for the block.
.decl ccs_flag_reset(a: node, f: node)
ccs_flag_reset(a, f) :- ccs_post_assign(f, a, l, r), (kind(l, "attribute") ; kind(l, "subscript")), text(l, d),
    ccs_flag(r, k), ccs_pre_flag(f, d, k0), k != k0.
.decl ccs_pre_flag(f: node, d: symbol, k: symbol)
ccs_pre_flag(f, d, k) :- ccs_pre_assign(f, _, l, r), text(l, d), ccs_flag(r, k).
.decl ccs_flag(r: node, k: symbol)
ccs_flag(r, "true") :- kind(r, "true").
ccs_flag(r, "false") :- kind(r, "false").
ccs_flag(r, "none") :- kind(r, "none").
// ccs_environ_write(s, f): a write to os.environ in f's own frame: an item assignment, a del, pop() or update().
.decl ccs_environ_write(s: node, f: node)
ccs_environ_write(a, f) :- ccs_assign(f, a, l, _), kind(l, "subscript"), field(l, "value", e), sym_of(e, "os.environ").
ccs_environ_write(d, f) :- kind(d, "delete_statement"), pp_frame(d, f), pp_cm_def(f), within(l, d),
    kind(l, "subscript"), field(l, "value", e), sym_of(e, "os.environ").
ccs_environ_write(c, f) :- ccs_call_in(c, f), field(c, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, e, m), (m = "pop" ; m = "update"),
    sym_of(e, "os.environ").

// ---- del of what the def set -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ccs_unset(d, f): `del T` (T an attribute or subscript) or `delattr(o, "a")` in f's own frame, after a yield of f
// before which f set T (`T = v`, also as one target of `T, x = v, w`, or `setattr(o, "a", v)`), compared by text.
.decl ccs_unset(d: node, f: node)
ccs_unset(d, f) :- kind(d, "delete_statement"), pp_frame(d, f), pp_cm_def(f), ccs_del_target(d, n),
    (kind(n, "attribute") ; kind(n, "subscript")), text(n, x), ccs_pre_target(f, x, y), earlier(y, d).
ccs_unset(c, f) :- ccs_call_in(c, f), field(c, "function", fn), sym_of(fn, "builtins.delattr"), ccs_attr_key(c, x),
    ccs_pre_target(f, x, y), earlier(y, c).
.decl ccs_del_target(d: node, n: node)
ccs_del_target(d, n) :- kind(d, "delete_statement"), child(d, n, _), !kind(n, "expression_list").
ccs_del_target(d, n) :- kind(d, "delete_statement"), child(d, l, _), kind(l, "expression_list"), child(l, n, _).
// ccs_pre_target(f, x, y): before yield y, f set the attribute or subscript written x.
.decl ccs_pre_target(f: node, x: symbol, y: node)
ccs_pre_target(f, x, y) :- ccs_assign(f, a, l, _), (n = l ; child(l, n, _)), (kind(n, "attribute") ; kind(n, "subscript")),
    text(n, x), pp_cm_yield(y, f), earlier(a, y).
ccs_pre_target(f, x, y) :- ccs_call_in(c, f), field(c, "function", fn), sym_of(fn, "builtins.setattr"),
    ccs_attr_key(c, x), pp_cm_yield(y, f), earlier(c, y).
// ccs_attr_key(c, x): `setattr(o, "a", ...)` or `delattr(o, "a")` names the attribute written x, `o.a`.
.decl ccs_attr_key(c: node, x: symbol)
ccs_attr_key(c, cat(cat(ot, "."), an)) :- ccs_call_in(c, _), posarg(c, 0, o), posarg(c, 1, s), text(o, ot),
    str_const(s, an).

// ---- removal from a container the def added to -------------------------------------------------------------------
// ccs_unregister(c, f): `X.remove(...)` and the other remove verbs after a yield of f, before which f called an add
// verb on X (by X's text); or `X.pop(k)` after f set `X[k]` before the yield.
.decl ccs_unregister(c: node, f: node)
ccs_unregister(c, f) :- ccs_call_in(c, f), field(c, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, o, m), ccs_remove_verb(m), text(o, d),
    ccs_pre_add(f, d, y), earlier(y, c).
ccs_unregister(c, f) :- ccs_call_in(c, f), field(c, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, o, "pop"), text(o, d), posarg(c, 0, k),
    text(k, kt), ccs_pre_item(f, d, kt, y), earlier(y, c).
.decl ccs_pre_add(f: node, d: symbol, y: node)
ccs_pre_add(f, d, y) :- ccs_call_in(c, f), field(c, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, o, m), ccs_add_verb(m), text(o, d),
    pp_cm_yield(y, f), earlier(c, y).
.decl ccs_pre_item(f: node, d: symbol, k: symbol, y: node)
ccs_pre_item(f, d, k, y) :- ccs_assign(f, a, l, _), (n = l ; child(l, n, _)), kind(n, "subscript"), field(n, "value", v),
    text(v, d), field(n, "subscript", s), text(s, k), pp_cm_yield(y, f), earlier(a, y).
.decl ccs_method_name(m: symbol)
ccs_method_name(m) :- ccs_call_in(c, _), field(c, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, _, m).
.decl ccs_add_verb(m: symbol)
ccs_add_verb(m) :- ccs_method_name(m),
    match("(append|appendleft|insert|add|extend|push|register|subscribe|attach|install)([A-Z_].*)?", m).
.decl ccs_remove_verb(m: symbol)
ccs_remove_verb(m) :- ccs_method_name(m),
    match("(remove|pop|popleft|discard|clear|unregister|unsubscribe|detach|uninstall)([A-Z_].*)?", m).

// ---- paired calls ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ccs_effect(c): call c is a statement of its own (or `await c` is): it is made for its effect, its value dropped.
.decl ccs_effect(c: node)
ccs_effect(c) :- ccs_call_in(c, _), pp_discarded(c).
ccs_effect(c) :- ccs_call_in(c, _), kind(w, "await"), child(w, c, 0), kind(s, "expression_statement"), child(s, e, 0),
    !child(s, _, 1), unparen(e, w).
// ccs_set_call(c, f, y): call c sets something before yield y of f: a statement of its own, or the whole value of
// an assignment (`old = signal.signal(s, h)`, which sets and returns the old state).
.decl ccs_set_call(c: node, f: node, y: node)
ccs_set_call(c, f, y) :- ccs_effect(c), ccs_call_in(c, f), pp_cm_yield(y, f), earlier(c, y).
ccs_set_call(c, f, y) :- ccs_assign(f, _, _, r), unparen(r, c), kind(c, "call"), pp_cm_yield(y, f), earlier(c, y).
ccs_set_call(c, f, y) :- ccs_assign(f, _, _, r), unparen(r, w), kind(w, "await"), child(w, c, 0), kind(c, "call"),
    pp_cm_yield(y, f), earlier(c, y).
// ccs_key(c, k): the function call c calls, by its resolved name, else by its dotted text (`self.set_level`).
.decl ccs_key(c: node, k: symbol)
ccs_key(c, q) :- ccs_call_in(c, _), field(c, "function", fn), sym_of(fn, q).
ccs_key(c, d) :- ccs_call_in(c, _), field(c, "function", fn), !sym_of(fn, _), dotted_expr(fn, d).
// ccs_computes(c): call c computes a value: it calls a builtin (str, int, len, print, ...) or a class of the run.
.decl ccs_computes(c: node)
ccs_computes(c) :- ccs_key(c, q), prefix("builtins.", q).
ccs_computes(c) :- ccs_key(c, q), class_def(_, q).
.decl ccs_nargs(c: node, n: number)
ccs_nargs(c, n) :- ccs_call_in(c, _), n = count : { posarg(c, _, _) }.
// ccs_pair(c0, c, f): c0 sets something before a yield of f, and c, a statement after that yield, calls the same
// function with as many positional arguments.
.decl ccs_pair(c0: node, c: node, f: node)
ccs_pair(c0, c, f) :- ccs_effect(c), ccs_call_in(c, f), ccs_key(c, k), !ccs_computes(c), ccs_set_call(c0, f, y),
    earlier(y, c), ccs_key(c0, k), ccs_nargs(c0, n), ccs_nargs(c, n).
// ccs_restore_call(c, f): the restore form: c passes, at one position, a name holding the state read before the
// set, where c0 passed something else, and the other positions are the same text.
.decl ccs_restore_call(c: node, f: node)
ccs_restore_call(c, f) :- ccs_pair(c0, c, f), posarg(c, i, a), kind(a, "identifier"), text(a, v), posarg(c0, i, a0),
    text(a0, t0), t0 != v, !ccs_other_differs(c0, c, i), ccs_saved_state(f, v, c0).
.decl ccs_other_differs(c0: node, c: node, i: number)
ccs_other_differs(c0, c, i) :- ccs_pair(c0, c, _), posarg(c, i, _), posarg(c, j, a), j != i, posarg(c0, j, a0),
    text(a, t), text(a0, t0), t != t0.
// ccs_saved_state(f, v, c0): name v is bound, before the set call c0 (or by it), to a read of state: a call that
// does not compute (a getter, or the setter returning the old value), an attribute or a subscript.
.decl ccs_saved_state(f: node, v: symbol, c0: node)
ccs_saved_state(f, v, c0) :- ccs_set_call(c0, f, _), ccs_assign(f, a, l, r0), kind(l, "identifier"), text(l, v),
    unparen(r0, r), ccs_read(r), (earlier(a, c0) ; within(c0, a)).
.decl ccs_read(r: node)
ccs_read(r) :- kind(r, "attribute").
ccs_read(r) :- kind(r, "subscript").
ccs_read(r) :- kind(r, "call"), !ccs_computed(r).
ccs_read(r) :- kind(r, "await"), child(r, c, 0), kind(c, "call").
// ccs_computed(r): call r computes a value rather than reading state: a builtin other than getattr, or a class of
// the run.
.decl ccs_computed(r: node)
ccs_computed(r) :- kind(r, "call"), field(r, "function", fn), sym_of(fn, q), prefix("builtins.", q),
    q != "builtins.getattr".
ccs_computed(r) :- kind(r, "call"), field(r, "function", fn), sym_of(fn, q), class_def(_, q).
// ccs_reset_call(c, f): the reset form: every argument of c is a neutral constant, and c0 passed other arguments.
.decl ccs_reset_call(c: node, f: node)
ccs_reset_call(c, f) :- ccs_pair(c0, c, f), posarg(c, _, _), !ccs_live_arg(c), field(c, "arguments", l),
    field(c0, "arguments", l0), text(l, t), text(l0, t0), t != t0.
// ccs_live_arg(c): c passes an argument that is not a neutral constant (a keyword argument counts as one).
.decl ccs_live_arg(c: node)
ccs_live_arg(c) :- ccs_effect(c), field(c, "arguments", l), child(l, a, _), !kind(a, "comment"), !ccs_neutral(a).
// ccs_neutral(a): 0, None, False, or a named constant (a name or attribute whose last name is in capitals:
// logging.NOTSET, signal.SIG_DFL).
.decl ccs_neutral(a: node)
ccs_neutral(a) :- kind(a, "integer"), text(a, "0").
ccs_neutral(a) :- kind(a, "none").
ccs_neutral(a) :- kind(a, "false").
ccs_neutral(a) :- (kind(a, "identifier") ; kind(a, "attribute")), leaf_name(a, x), match("[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]+", x).

